{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"9a68bc785ed90b6c167c1633cdcfbeb690546a2816d9162fdb38d4d38404bb39","packTokens":2342,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":252,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":542,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1267,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"failures","tokens":167,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"A web front end with a small API and a database behind it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"The app ships with exactly 8 requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Requests are stored in the database and survive a reload and a restart.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The API needs these four operations and no others: list, create, get by ID, and change status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Requests screen with status filters, create dialog, and loading, empty, and error states.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Request detail screen with status-appropriate action, update failure state, and not-found state.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Clean light theme, responsive layout, accessible controls, and specified badge colors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Automated tests for the business rules and one end-to-end workflow.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"If the user creates a request while a status filter other than All is selected, how should the list behave after successful creation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Switch the filter to All so the new Open request appears at the top.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which browsers must the web app support?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No specific browser support target beyond browsers compatible with the chosen implementation.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If the create API call fails for a reason other than field validation, what should the dialog show?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show “Could not create request.” in the dialog, keep the entered values, and allow retry.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How should surrounding whitespace in a title affect requiredness, length validation, and the stored title?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Trim surrounding whitespace before validating and storing the title.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"After a successful status change on the detail screen, what should happen to the Requests list when the user returns to it?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the selected filter and refresh the list; the request may disappear if it no longer matches the filter.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the 1280 px table-layout target be configurable, or remain the fixed target specified for this release?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep 1280 px as the fixed table-layout target.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the request detail screen add states for loading a request and for failures other than not-found?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the specified detail behavior: show the request on success and “Request not found.” for an unknown ID; add no other fetch states.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a browser-accessible maintenance request system with a web front end, an HTTP API, and a database that stores request records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"On initialization of an empty database, seed exactly eight requests: four Open, including exactly one Urgent, two In progress, and two Done, with every supported area represented.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Persist request records across browser reloads and application restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Expose exactly four API operations: list requests, create a request, get a request by ID, and change a request's status; reject API attempts to edit fixed request fields or delete requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Return all requests, or requests matching one requested status, ordered newest first.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"On valid request creation, assign a system-generated ID and UTC creation time and set status to Open.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Validate creation fields: title trimmed to 3–80 characters, area of Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, or Reception, priority of Low, Normal, or Urgent, and optional description of at most 500 characters; reject invalid values with an error naming the field, and trim the title.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Keep title, area, priority, and description fixed after creation and reject attempts to change those fields or delete a request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Enforce status transitions Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open; reject other status changes, return not-found for an unknown request ID, and return an error without changing the request when the status body is missing or unrecognized.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Display the Hive Works wordmark, signed-in demo user initials SC, a status filter with All, Open, In progress, and Done choices with All initially selected, a New request button, and a newest-first request list on the Requests screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"When a user selects a status filter or returns from request detail, load the list for the selected filter and retain that filter on return from detail.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When New request is opened, show a dialog with Title, Area, Priority defaulting to Normal, and Description fields, plus Create and Cancel controls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"After valid request creation succeeds, close the dialog, select All, and show the new Open request at the top of the list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"When a create field fails validation, keep the dialog open and display the field's error under that field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"When creation fails for a non-validation reason, show “Could not create request.” in the dialog, retain entered values, and allow retry.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"While requests are loading, absent for the selected filter, or fail to load, display the corresponding loading, empty, or error state; provide retry for load errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"For an existing request, display a back link, title, area, priority badge, status badge, created date, and description or “No description.” when the description is empty.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Show Start work for Open, Mark done for In progress, and Reopen for Done on the request detail screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"After a successful status change, show the new status and corresponding action; on failure, show “Could not update the request.” and retain the prior status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"For an unknown request ID, display “Request not found.” and a link back to the Requests screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Use one light theme, one sans-serif font, a neutral background, near-black text, and specified status and priority badge colors with text labels on every badge: Open blue, In progress amber, Done green, Urgent red, and Low and Normal neutral.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Show request dates as date-only values, use stacked cards at 375 px and table rows at the fixed 1280 px target, avoid horizontal page scrolling at those widths, label every field, make every control keyboard reachable, and meet WCAG AA text contrast.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Display created dates as date-only values such as “8 Oct 2026,” without a time or timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Include automated tests for request business rules and an end-to-end list-to-completion workflow.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L3 ears] REQ-9 needs exactly one \"shall\"\n- [spec-lint L8 anchors] REQ-1 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-2 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-3 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-4 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-5 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-6 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-7 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-8 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code (+16 more)\n</failures>\n\nMap the sentences."}